  "body": "EOS and VOYAGER are parallel research branches with different formal pins. This draft compares their exact file/claim/source contracts and derives the finite action invariant behind EOS's opaque-label Heisenberg experiment, without importing or merging EOS files.\n\nFor every n\u22652, the specified A/B actions and z readout on (Z/nZ)^3 have a faithful order n^3 unitriangular action on the n^2-state behavioral quotient (y,z). The regular holonomy-killing cover and behavioral Schreier observer minimize different invariants. Readout-y and added-swap controls show why source noncommutation need not be observer-visible and why a new action can invalidate a previous quotient.\n\nThese are classical paper proofs and exact computational controls. Principal independent ring-matrix review survives. The opaque-label learner's supplied source family and commutator template are disclosed; academic originality and physical meaning are unclaimed. Branch baseline is VOYAGER5eb09e7, not EOS; Lean4.19 is not mixed with4.14. This scoped result is also integrated into the rolling atlas in draft PR49, and is separated here for review of the sibling audit and finite algebra.\n\nValidation: exact moduli2\u20137 probe, file/claim comparison, and principal fresh ring controls pass. The integration branch passed full repository CI and provenance; this child branch's redundant baseline CI was cancelled to conserve quota and is not reported as passed. No imported/archive/default/main changes.\n",
